Hi,

This simple app breaks GAE when trying to return the 304 (GAE instance breaks with a server error "The server encountered an error and could not complete your request.") (the first request works, and return the 200, but the second always breaks)

With all versions of Starlette, except the **"0.8.1"** ... (so I stay in 0.8.1, and can't upgrade)

```python
import uvicorn
from starlette.applications import Starlette
from starlette.responses import Response

app = Starlette()
###############################################################################
@app.route('/',methods=["GET"])
def test(request):
    if "myetag"!=request.headers.get("if-none-match",None):
        return Response(status_code=200,content="hello",headers={"Content-Type":"text/plain","etag":"myetag"})
    else:
        return Response(status_code=304)

if __name__=="__main__":
    uvicorn.run(app, host="0.0.0.0", port=8080)
```

What's happening since 0.8.1 ?
I really like to upgrade to newer version, but I stick with a working one ;-(
